      <section id="description-section" class="product-anchor-section">
        <h1>Product Details</h1>
        <div>
          <p>Build a welding table that will transform your workshop. This is the official technical documentation for the table you know from the Mateusz Doniec channel. This project is not just a “drawing” — it is the result of combining Mateusz’s practical workshop experience with the 20 years of experience of our technologist. You receive a proven, stable and highly precise construction that you can build for a fraction of the market price.
          </p>

<h3>Why choose the dWT02 project?</h3>
<p>By purchasing this product, you receive complete documentation (DXF and PDF files):</p>

<ul class="dots">
    <li>
        <p><b>2000x1000 mm size:</b>&nbsp;An ideal working surface for medium-length profiles, frames and gate constructions.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>Full mobility:</b>&nbsp;Thanks to its own wheel system, once the work is done, you can move the table back against the wall and regain space in your garage.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>System 16/28 compatibility:</b>&nbsp;Plans are available for both standards — choose the version that matches your tools.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
        <p><b>Material flexibility:</b>&nbsp;The project is prepared for 10,12 and 15mm thick steel plates. You decide on the balance between rigidity and budget.</p>
    </li> 
    <li>
        <p><b>“Building block” assembly:</b>&nbsp;Precise DXF files for laser cutting make the build simple, fast and possible without specialist machinery.</p>
    </li>
</ul>

            <h3>What does this project include?</h3>

          <ul class="dots">
                 <li>
                  <p><b>Precise DXF files:</b>&nbsp;Ready for laser cutting and designed to keep material waste to a minimum.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Detailed assembly manual (PDF):</b>&nbsp;A clear step-by-step guide that makes preparation and assembly of all parts easier.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Complete material list:</b>&nbsp;A detailed breakdown of the steel plate thicknesses and steel grades required to build the complete set.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Technical documentation and 3D views:</b>&nbsp;Clear assembly drawings that make fabrication and assembly easier.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>​BONUS:</b>&nbsp;Behind-the-scenes photos from the welding table build at Mateusz Doniec’s workshop.</p>
                </li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Why is this set worth choosing?</h3>

          <ul class="dots">
                <li>
                  <p><b>Project verified in real workshop use:</b>&nbsp;Every element of this table has proven itself in Mateusz Doniec’s workshop.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Proven workshop solutions:</b>&nbsp;The project was created based on real workshop needs and hands-on experience with welding table work.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>Complete project in one place:</b>&nbsp;DXF files, PDF manual, material list and technical drawings — everything you need to build the set.</p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p><b>A fraction of the market price:</b>&nbsp;Building the table yourself can save you thousands compared to buying ready-made professional products.</p>
                </li>
                 <li>
                  <p><b>Time saving:</b>&nbsp;You receive ready-made documentation that helps you prepare parts for production and assembly faster.</p>
                </li>
              </ul>
               </div>

        <div class="product-note">
  <p class="product-note__title">ℹ️ Digital Product (DIY Plans)</p>
  <p>This product is digital documentation — a complete set of welding table build plans. It does not include physical accessories, metal parts or a finished table. To complete the project properly, basic welding skills are required, as well as ordering the steel parts to be cut according to the included DXF files, for example by laser or plasma cutting.</p>
</div>
